.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NQWIPE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqwipe
.Nd erase secret data from memory
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft void
.Fn nqwipe "void *p" "size_t len"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqwipe
sets the
.Fa len
bytes at
.Fa p
to zero in a way the compiler cannot remove as dead stores, even just
before the memory is freed or goes out of scope: with C23's
.Fn memset_explicit
when the library is built as C23 or later and the C library has it,
and otherwise through a volatile pointer.
.Fa p
may be
.Dv NULL ,
and then nothing happens.
.Pp
The library wipes every secret it holds (keys, seeds, shared secrets,
intermediate state, freed memory of the capsule layer) before it
returns, on every path.
Callers wipe their own copies: secret keys, seeds and shared secrets they
no longer need.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
None.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static uint8_t sk[4032];
/* ... sign with sk ... */
nqwipe(sk, sizeof sk);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr explicit_bzero 3 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqcteq 3
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn nqwipe
cannot erase copies outside the buffer it is given: registers, swap,
core dumps or copies the caller made.
